  "term": "comparative analysis",
  "definition": "Comparative analysis here means understanding something by comparing two kinds of being, especially self-existent or essential being with derived being. In the passage, it is the method used to describe the first cause by noting what creatures have in a limited way and then distinguishing the uncaused source from those limitations.",
